  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659746",
      "title": "When Should You Split Components?",
      "sourceHash": "aadff34bfa15a667761b32581477cffbcaa0c4e5ced716f2e7d330d87d161c1b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "Next, let's focus on Components again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 5.16,
          "en": "And for that, still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.16,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "in that same project still in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "If we take a look at this JSX code in there, we can see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "in that root component, we got a lot of things going on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 21.36,
          "en": "A lot of different responsibilities in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "because this app component is actually responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "for rendering this core concepts section here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "and all these core concept items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "And it's also responsible for managing these tap buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 41.16,
          "en": "and this interactive part at the bottom of the screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.16,
          "end": 43.98,
          "en": "All these things are in the end managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "by this app component, and that's why this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 50.61,
          "en": "app component manages both this state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.61,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "for this interactive area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "and also has to import this core concept data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 58.323,
          "en": "from the data js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 61.59,
          "en": "Now of course, for this basic app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "that's not necessarily a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "but having a single component that deals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 70.889,
          "en": "with such different things typically is a sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.889,
          "end": 73.02,
          "en": "that you might want to split it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 78.02,
          "en": "up and break it up into multiple smaller sub Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.09,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "And in this app specifically here, there also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 84.9,
          "en": "is another sign because you might've noticed that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 89.67,
          "en": "if I click one of these tap buttons occasionally this text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 91.83,
          "en": "up here changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.83,
          "end": 95.75999999999999,
          "en": "So as I click this here, you see it changes to fundamental",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.75999999999999,
          "end": 99.12,
          "en": "and then here to crucial and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "And this happens because we're managing this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "This selected topic state in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "And as you learned in the previous section, whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.82,
          "en": "this state is updated with help of this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.82,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "state updating function here, the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "to which this state belongs is re-executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "sp that React is able to find out if something changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 128.853,
          "en": "about this JSX code and is able to update the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 134.34,
          "en": "But since this header component here is of course being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.34,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "in this app component, this header component function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "is also re-executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 142.92000000000002,
          "en": "Because this entire code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.92000000000002,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "in the app component is re-executed when the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 148.77,
          "en": "app component function is executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 151.26,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, the header component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "is also called again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 156.75,
          "en": "And in there, and therefore generating a new random number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "every time this is drawn again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 161.46,
          "en": "And I'm updating this text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "And this is another signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 166.14,
          "en": "that maybe we're managing the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.14,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "this selected topic state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "in the wrong component and that we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 173.22,
          "en": "might wanna split up this app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.22,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "and that's therefore what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 178.77,
          "en": "Because being able to identify good",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 183,
          "en": "places for extra Components and being able to split",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "up your big Components into smaller Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 190.38,
          "en": "and to separate responsibilities is an important skill",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.38,
          "end": 192.543,
          "en": "for every React developer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}